Yes, it boils down to that.
The mean is just: mean = sum/n, where sum is the necessary level changes
over all n samples. The second data line counts level change attempts
while you're on a non-teleport level. (Whether you use gain level or the
stairs is not relevant the way I derived it here; you have to pass the
levels [on average] that often, and it's up to the operator to decide
whether the stairs should be used or potions should be better applied,
since The Force can pop by either way of level change.)

