Well, I suppose it's partly depending on the small sample set n; if I run
that (for a depth of 22 dlevels) with n=10000 I get an value of 17.5 non-
teleport levels that the character has to pass.

What's to consider as well, though, is the observable variance. The column
named max also gives hints on that; if in 50 games you have one where you
have to traverse 39 (or even 45) times a non-teleport level is certainly
tough and bad luck.

> 
