> be able to ascend within 1200 turns of killing Rodney if the mysterious
> force annoys you at only an average rate.

With n=10000, #dlvls=22, I get an average of ~48 levels necessary to pass
(20.5 teleportable levels and 17.5 non-teleport levels).

I use scrolls of teleportation for the teleportable levels, gain level for
the levels which have long ways (primarily Asmodeus), and just walk if the
up-/down-stairs are comparably nearby. (We have also to take into account
that teleport may also just fail a couple of times.) So the use of potions,
or scrolls depend on the amount I have collected and the maze layout WRT
stairs; if I have resources in abundance I use teleport also to bridge
mid-range stairs-distances, while if resources are scarce I just walk and
save the scrolls and any potions for the larger distances.

Often my resources fit to pass Gehennom conveniently, not uncommon that I
have some spare scrolls of teleport for the upper dungeons as well, and
rarely I have spare potions to use even in the upper dungeons, say to pass
Titan's variant of Medusa's Level quickly as well. To escape the convoluted
Valley is, BTW, also a very appropriate application for a potion.

